                    },
                    "message": "Critical test logic error - testing wrong power state\nLocation: Lines 146-152 in gui/gui_test/operations_menu/test_firmware_sub_menu.robot\n\nIssue: Test claims to verify power-ON state but setup powers OFF the server and never powers it ON. The test is actually verifying power-OFF behavior, not power-ON as documented and named.\nExpected Behavior: At power-ON state (line 131), the switch button should be DISABLED. At power-OFF state (line 69), the button should be VISIBLE/ENABLED.\nFix: Change setup to Power On Server to actually test power-ON state as intended\nWhy: This is a critical functional test error. The test name, documentation, and tag all indicate power-ON testing, but the implementation tests power-OFF state. This makes the test meaningless and could mask real bugs in power-ON state handling."
